  "details": "I was sitting in an instance when I got disconnected for whatever reason. The log has the disconnect in it if you search for \"OnDisconnected\". Seems like a random network error but when I rejoined automatically, I had a weird blue circle in the center of my screen (Img attached). After looking around, it disappeared from my view after I had opened my camera. Then I checked the camera from the back and it matches the image I saw. It seems something like the forced reconnect caused the camera to lose it's position and anchor into my skull. The camera settings I had been using were the Stream camera anchored to \"Local\" and spout enabled. This all happened while I was on desktop.\n\nLog: https://gist.github.com/NighthawkVRC/589f4ae7acf801c13acbbb5782c6d5c0",
